exactly distance \code{eps}) are its neighbors.
\subsection{Sorting and self-matches}{
\itemize{
\item \strong{Sorting:} With \code{sort = TRUE} (default), the neighbors of each point are
ordered by increasing distance and ties are broken by id. With
\code{sort = FALSE}, the neighbors are returned in no particular order, which
avoids the cost of sorting. A \code{frNN} object can be sorted later using \code{sort()}.
\item \strong{Self-matches:} If no \code{query} is specified, then self-matches are
removed. If \code{query} is specified, then a query point that is also in \code{x}
is returned as its own neighbor (at distance 0).
}
