\subsection{Using a frNN object as \code{x}}{

If \code{x} is a \code{frNN} object, then the neighborhoods are reduced to the
smaller radius \code{eps}. An error is raised if \code{eps} is larger than the radius
stored in \code{x}. All other arguments are ignored.
}

