\itemize{
\item \code{x} can be a numeric matrix, a data.frame with only numeric columns, a
\link{dist} object or a \code{frNN} object.
\item \code{query} needs to be a numeric matrix or data.frame with the same number of
columns as \code{x}, and can only be used if \code{x} is a data matrix.
}
}

\subsection{Memory}{

The size of the result grows with the number of neighbors of all points, which
can approach \eqn{O(n^2)} for a large \code{eps}. Choose \code{eps} carefully for large
data sets.
}

