\code{shrinkRule} applies only to bd trees (\code{"none"} gives a tree that
behaves like a k-d tree).
\item \code{approx} uses the approximate fixed-radius search implemented in ANN.
All neighbors up to a distance of \code{eps / (1 + approx)} are considered
